Hi Daniel!

The benchmarks I did apply to my test case (2cmt oral PK model). I would recommend (in order of importance):

1. Keep integrate_ode with the RK45 for non-stiff
2. replace integrate_ode_cvode with a CVODES based stiff solver
3. Add a further integrate_ode function which allows to set abs+rel tol and maximum number of steps
4. use code from step 2 to refactor integrate_ode in order to have less code to maintain to go forward
5. consider exposing the adams_moulton of CVODES - I am sure some models will benefit from this

We still need to decide of how to name those functions; to be discussed Tuesday?

Sebastian

